# 📥 Indeed CV Downloader

Bulk download CVs from your Indeed job postings → upload to Google Drive → view a searchable database. **100% free to run.**

---

## What It Does

1. You paste your Indeed session cookies
2. App scrapes all applicant CVs from your job posting
3. Every CV is uploaded to your Google Drive folder
4. You get a searchable table of all candidates with direct Drive links

---

## Setup (One Time)

### 1. Clone & Install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/indeed-cv-downloader
cd indeed-cv-downloader
npm install
```

### 2. Google Service Account (Free)

1. Go to [console.cloud.google.com](https://console.cloud.google.com/)
2. Create a new project
3. Enable **Google Drive API**: APIs & Services → Enable APIs → search "Drive API" → Enable
4. Create a Service Account:
   - APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → Service Account
   - Name it anything (e.g. `cv-downloader`) → Done
5. Create a JSON key:
   - Click your service account → Keys tab → Add Key → Create new key → JSON → Download
6. **Share your Google Drive folder** with the service account:
   - Open your target folder in Drive
   - Click Share → paste the service account email (e.g. `cv-downloader@myproject.iam.gserviceaccount.com`)
   - Set to **Editor** → Share

### 3. Set Environment Variable

Open `.env.local` and paste the entire contents of your downloaded JSON file as one line:

```
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"my-proj",...}
```

### 4. Deploy to Vercel

```bash
npm install -g vercel
vercel --prod
```

In **Vercel Dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables**, add:
- `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` → paste the full JSON string

---

## How to Get Indeed Cookies

1. Log in to [employers.indeed.com](https://employers.indeed.com) in Chrome
2. Press `F12` → **Application** tab → **Cookies** → `https://employers.indeed.com`
3. Right-click any cookie → **Copy All as JSON**
4. Paste into the app

> ⚠️ Cookies expire after a session. Re-copy if downloads fail.

---

## How to Find Your Job URL

1. Go to [employers.indeed.com](https://employers.indeed.com)
2. Click your job → **Candidates** tab
3. Copy the URL — it looks like:
   `https://employers.indeed.com/jobs/12345678/candidates`

---

## Google Drive Folder ID

The folder ID is in the URL when you open a folder:
```
https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/THIS_IS_THE_FOLDER_ID
```

---

## Local Dev

```bash
npm run dev
# Open http://localhost:3000
```

---

## Cost

**$0.** Google Drive API is free. Vercel free tier is sufficient. No AI, no paid APIs.
